# One shape of `printf`, in its own module, through a door of its own.
#
# The C symbol is `printf`, the same symbol `as_text.hero` reaches at another
# shape. Until 2026-11-10 this module bound it directly, `printf(format: cstr
# lent, value: i64)`, and was called with `"n = %d\n"`: past `printf`'s `...`
# nothing held `value` to the `int` `%d` reads, and 4294967338 printed
# `n = 42`. A binding declares no parameter past a header's `...` since panel
# 243's R1 (defect 2421), so `as_int.h` defines `say_count`, a function of a
# new name with a fixed prototype holding the literal format, and this group
# binds that.

extern "as_int.h"
    function say_count(n: i64) -> i32

# The route out of the module, because an `extern` is never callable
# across a module boundary (acceptance row 1, panel 033 R5).
function say(value: i64) -> i32
    return say_count(n: value)
